WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:02.653
- The nominees for Best
Performance by an Actress

00:00:02.653 --> 00:00:04.475
in a Leading Role in a
Play, Lauren Ridloff,

00:00:04.475 --> 00:00:06.558
Children of a Lesser God.

00:00:07.166 --> 00:00:12.166
(applause) (gentle, ambient music)

00:00:15.159 --> 00:00:17.317
- The first time that I was introduced

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.609
to Children of a Lesser
God was when I was eight.

00:00:19.609 --> 00:00:22.675
The movie came out and my parents decided

00:00:22.675 --> 00:00:24.994
to take me to see the movie even though

00:00:24.994 --> 00:00:27.327
they knew it was for adults.

00:00:37.496 --> 00:00:39.520
It had a huge impact on me to see

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:42.603
another deaf adult on the big screen.

00:00:42.907 --> 00:00:46.490
I never once thought
that I would be Sarah.

00:00:47.542 --> 00:00:49.407
First of all, I'm a woman of color,

00:00:49.407 --> 00:00:52.574
and I just assumed that it was a given

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:55.390
that Sarah was going to be white.

00:00:55.768 --> 00:00:59.101
(gentle, ambient music)

00:01:01.641 --> 00:01:05.641
I was a school teacher,
so I taught kindergarten

00:01:06.585 --> 00:01:09.222
and first grade in public education.

00:01:09.222 --> 00:01:13.139
Every day I had to read
aloud with my students,

00:01:14.008 --> 00:01:16.674
and that always involves acting in a way.

00:01:16.674 --> 00:01:19.257
And a tough audience, children.

00:01:20.798 --> 00:01:24.215
And then I left to raise my own two boys.

00:01:24.244 --> 00:01:26.922
Kenny was presented with the possibility

00:01:26.922 --> 00:01:29.721
of doing a revival of
Children of a Lesser God,

00:01:29.721 --> 00:01:31.365
and he decided that he wanted

00:01:31.365 --> 00:01:33.243
to meet a person who was deaf first.

00:01:33.243 --> 00:01:34.826
So he contacted me.

00:01:34.969 --> 00:01:36.656
We set up a time to meet.

00:01:36.656 --> 00:01:39.586
Then we set up a plan to meet once a week

00:01:39.586 --> 00:01:41.846
for a year and we would
talk about deaf culture,

00:01:41.846 --> 00:01:43.797
I would teach him some signs...

00:01:43.797 --> 00:01:46.075
So, after a year of meeting,

00:01:46.075 --> 00:01:49.742
and I was his teacher
and he was my student,

00:01:49.827 --> 00:01:52.543
he then asked me to be a participant

00:01:52.543 --> 00:01:55.395
in the first reading with Joshua Jackson.

00:01:55.395 --> 00:01:59.031
After that reading was over,
he pulled me aside and said,

00:01:59.031 --> 00:02:00.619
"If this goes all the way,

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:03.189
are you willing to go all the way?"

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.689
And my answer is pretty clear.

00:02:09.811 --> 00:02:11.719
And working with Joshua Jackson

00:02:11.719 --> 00:02:13.906
made the whole process so easy.

00:02:13.906 --> 00:02:14.947
He's such a veteran.

00:02:14.947 --> 00:02:18.197
He's been in this industry for so long.

00:02:26.285 --> 00:02:28.968
This story holds such a special place

00:02:28.968 --> 00:02:32.063
for the deaf community. It opened doors

00:02:32.063 --> 00:02:35.813
to Broadway back when
it first was performed.

00:02:35.859 --> 00:02:37.988
We definitely have a long way to go

00:02:37.988 --> 00:02:41.238
regarding inclusivity in this business.

00:02:41.758 --> 00:02:44.803
When you hear the word
inclusion in this industry,

00:02:44.803 --> 00:02:47.080
it tends to focus on
color and I think we need

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:51.997
to broaden that to people with
different abilities as well.

00:02:52.853 --> 00:02:55.020
It makes us better people.

00:02:55.604 --> 00:03:00.604
Once your eyes are opened and
you're exposed to differences,

00:03:01.021 --> 00:03:04.521
different ways of living, different ideas,

00:03:04.631 --> 00:03:06.381
you're feelings grow.

00:03:07.913 --> 00:03:10.393
And once you're exposed
to something like that,

00:03:10.393 --> 00:03:13.474
you can't go back, you
can only move forward.

00:03:13.474 --> 00:03:16.405
So I think it's really
important to meet people,

00:03:16.405 --> 00:03:18.076
to hear their stories, especially

00:03:18.076 --> 00:03:20.720
if their stories are not like yours.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:25.387
Because when you do, you find
that universal connection.

00:03:25.586 --> 00:03:29.503
(inspiring instrumental music)

